import { Meta, Canvas, Story, Source } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';
import * as BarListChartStories from './index.stories';

<Meta title="JS Packages/Charts Library/Charts/Bar List Chart" of={ BarListChartStories } />

# Bar List Chart

A specialized horizontal bar chart component that displays data as a ranked list with labels and values positioned alongside the bars. Ideal for showing comparisons between categories or time periods.

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.Default } />

## Overview

The BarListChart component extends the BarChart component to create a list-style visualization that combines horizontal bars with text labels and values. It automatically handles positioning of labels on the left and values on the right, making it perfect for dashboards and reports that need to display ranked data clearly.

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `import { BarListChart } from '@automattic/charts';
import '@automattic/charts/style.css';

	const data = [
		{
			group: 'primary',
			label: 'Sales By Product',
			data: [
				{ label: 'Product A', value: 32400 },
				{ label: 'Product B', value: 20000 },
				{ label: 'Product C', value: 15000 },
			],
		},
	];

	<BarListChart data={ data } />` }
/>

Key features:
- Automatic label and value positioning
- Support for single and multi-series data
- Customizable formatters for labels and values
- Custom component rendering for advanced styling
- Responsive design with automatic sizing

## API Reference

For detailed information about component props, types, and method signatures, see the [Bar List Chart API Reference](./?path=/docs/js-packages-charts-library-charts-bar-list-chart-api-reference--docs).

## Basic Usage

### Single Series Data

The simplest implementation displays a single series of data with automatic formatting:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.Default } />

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `const singleSeriesData = [
		{
			group: 'primary',
			label: 'Sales By Product',
			data: [
				{ label: 'Behemoth hat', value: 32400 },
				{ label: 'Margarita top', value: 20000 },
				{ label: 'Berlioz dress', value: 15000 },
				{ label: 'Woland shirt', value: 16000 },
			],
		},
	];

	<BarListChart
		data={ singleSeriesData }
		withTooltips={ true }
	/>` }
/>

### Multi-Series Data

Compare data across different time periods or categories:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.MultiSeries } />

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `const multiSeriesData = [
		{
			group: 'primary',
			label: 'Jan 21-Aug 8, 2024',
			data: [
				{ label: 'Organic search', value: 30000 },
				{ label: 'Affiliates', value: 19000 },
				{ label: 'Display', value: 18000 },
			],
		},
		{
			group: 'comparison',
			label: 'Jan 21-Aug 8, 2023',
			data: [
				{ label: 'Organic search', value: 20000 },
				{ label: 'Affiliates', value: 15000 },
				{ label: 'Display', value: 19900 },
			],
		},
	];

	<BarListChart data={ multiSeriesData } />` }
/>

### Required Props

- **`data`**: Array of SeriesData objects containing the chart data

For detailed prop information and configuration options, see the [Bar List Chart API Reference](./?path=/docs/js-packages-charts-library-charts-bar-list-chart-api-reference--docs).

## Chart Types

### Single Series (Default)

Best for displaying a simple ranked list of items:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.Default } />

Characteristics:
- Compact layout with minimal padding
- Labels positioned closer to bars
- Values displayed with compact number formatting
- Ideal for product rankings, performance metrics

### Multi-Series Comparison

Perfect for comparing data across time periods or categories:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.MultiSeries } />

Characteristics:
- Increased padding for better visual separation
- Grouped bars for comparison
- Automatic calculation of totals for value display
- Color coding based on series groups

## Styling and Customization

### Custom Label Components

Create custom label rendering with icons or enhanced styling:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.CustomLabelComponent } />

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `import { Circle } from '@visx/shape';
	import { Text } from '@visx/text';

	<BarListChart
		data={ data }
		options={ {
			labelComponent: ( { textProps, x, y, label, formatter } ) => (
				<>
					<Circle cx={ x + 6 } cy={ y } r={ 8 } />
					<Text
						{ ...textProps }
						textAnchor="start"
						x={ x + 24 }
						y={ y }
						fontWeight={ 500 }
					>
						{ formatter( label ) }
					</Text>
				</>
			),
		} }
	/>` }
/>

### Custom Value Components

Display additional information alongside values:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.CustomValueComponent } />

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `<BarListChart
		data={ data }
		options={ {
			valueComponent: ( { textProps, x, y, value, formatter, data, index } ) => {
				const currentValue = data[0].data[index].value;
				const previousValue = data[1].data[index].value;
				const percentage = previousValue === 0 ? 0 :
					(((currentValue - previousValue) / previousValue) * 100).toFixed(0);

				return (
					<>
						<Text
							{ ...textProps }
							textAnchor="end"
							x={ x }
							y={ y }
							dx={ -50 }
							fontWeight={ 500 }
						>
							{ formatter( value ) }
						</Text>
						<Text
							{ ...textProps }
							textAnchor="end"
							x={ x }
							y={ y }
							dx={ -10 }
							fill="#008A20"
							fontWeight={ 500 }
						>
							{ \`\${ Number( percentage ) > 0 ? '+' : '' }\${ percentage }%\` }
						</Text>
					</>
				);
			},
			valueFormatter: ( value ) => \`$\${ formatNumberCompact( value ) }\`,
		} }
	/>` }
/>

### Formatting Options

The `options` prop accepts various formatting and positioning controls:

#### `labelFormatter`

Controls how labels are displayed:

```jsx
options: {
	labelFormatter: (value) => value.toUpperCase()
}
```

#### `valueFormatter`

Controls how values are formatted:

```jsx
options: {
	valueFormatter: (value) => `$${formatNumberCompact(value)}`
}
```

#### `labelPosition` and `valuePosition`

Control the horizontal positioning of text elements:

```jsx
options: {
	labelPosition: 20,    // X position for labels
	valuePosition: 400,   // X position for values
}
```

## Theming Integration

Bar List Charts integrate seamlessly with the chart theming system. The default theme has neutral colors and styling, and is automatically applied to all charts unless a custom theme is provided. A custom theme can be provided by wrapping your chart in `GlobalChartsProvider` and passing a custom theme object with the properties you want to override to the `theme` prop:

<Source
	language="tsx"
	code={ `import { GlobalChartsProvider, BarListChart, type ChartTheme } from '@automattic/charts';

	const customTheme: ChartTheme = {
		colors: ['#FF6B6B', '#4ECDC4', '#45B7D1', '#FFA07A'],
	};

	<GlobalChartsProvider theme={customTheme}>
		<BarListChart data={data} />
	</GlobalChartsProvider>` }
/>

## Responsive Behavior

By default, BarListChart **fills its parent container's dimensions**. The parent must have an explicit height:

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `// Fill parent container (default) - parent needs explicit height
	<div style={{ width: '100%', height: '300px' }}>
		<BarListChart data={data} />
	</div>

	// Use aspect ratio - height calculated from width
	<div style={{ width: '100%' }}>
		<BarListChart data={data} aspectRatio={0.4} />
	</div>

	// Fixed dimensions
	<BarListChart data={data} width={600} height={300} />` }
/>

For more details on responsive behavior, see the [Responsive Design section](./?path=/docs/js-packages-charts-library-introduction--docs#responsive-design) in the introduction.

## Animation

The Bar List Chart component supports an optional entry animation that creates a smooth reveal effect when the chart first renders:

<Canvas of={ BarListChartStories.Animation } />

<Source
	language="tsx"
	code={ `<BarListChart
		data={ data }
		animation={ true }
	/>` }
/>

### Animation Behavior

- **Opt-in**: Animation is disabled by default and must be explicitly enabled with the `animation` prop
- **Accessibility**: Automatically respects the user's `prefers-reduced-motion` system setting - animation will not play for users who prefer reduced motion
- **Effect**: Creates a stretching effect where bars grow from left to right, revealing the data progressively
- **Duration**: 1000ms (1 second) with ease-out timing

**Note**: The animation plays once when the chart initially renders and does not repeat.

## Advanced Features

### Scale Configuration

Customize the chart scales for precise control over bar sizing and spacing:

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `<BarListChart
		data={ data }
		options={ {
			yScale: {
				paddingInner: 0.4,  // Space between bars
				padding: 0.2,       // Outer padding
			},
			xScale: {
				zero: true,         // Always start from zero
			},
		} }
	/>` }
/>

### Automatic Layout Calculation

The component automatically calculates optimal positioning based on:
- Number of data series (single vs multi-series)
- Chart dimensions
- Content overflow considerations

For multi-series charts, the component automatically adjusts:
- Bar thickness and spacing
- Label positioning
- Y-offset calculations for proper text alignment

### Custom Positioning

Override automatic positioning when needed:

<Source
	language="jsx"
	code={ `<BarListChart
		data={ data }
		options={ {
			yOffset: -20,          // Vertical offset for text
			labelPosition: 10,     // Fixed label position
			valuePosition: 380,    // Fixed value position
		} }
	/>` }
/>

## Accessibility

BarListChart inherits accessibility features from the underlying BarChart component, including keyboard navigation support when tooltips are enabled and proper ARIA attributes for screen readers.

## Migration from Bar Chart

If you're currently using a horizontal BarChart for list-style data, BarListChart provides a more optimized experience:

<Source language="jsx" code={`
	// Old approach with BarChart
	<BarChart
		orientation="horizontal"
		data={ data }
		// Complex custom axis configuration needed
		options={ {
			axis: {
				y: { /* complex custom renderer */ },
				x: { children: () => null }
			}
		} }
	/>

	// New approach with BarListChart
	<BarListChart data={ data } />
	`}
/>

Benefits of migration:
- Automatic label and value positioning
- Built-in formatting with sensible defaults
- Simplified API for common use cases

